                <pb facs="0265" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">368.117/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-17T14:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 18—4:19
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Legation’s telegram 274, December 23rd 1920 and Department’s 3, January 8th.
                    Naturalized Greeks desiring to return to America are having less difficulty in
                    getting their passports visaed by Greek authorities but up to the present in
                    spite of protests by former American Minister, the Greek Government has not
                    returned to the Legation any of the American passports which were seized.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
